{"step_index":135,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T00:07:05Z","thinking":"**Identifying Industry Classification**\n\nAnalyzing the provided data, the industry classification appears to be \"기어 및 동력전달장치 제조업\" (Gear and Power Transmission Equipment Manufacturing). This corresponds to the National Tax Service Industry Classification system, indicating a specific manufacturing sector. The associated phone number is \"055-342-2388,\" though fax and homepage information are missing.\n\n\n**Formulating Batch Enrichment Strategy**\n\nThe user's explicit instruction to avoid Excel access necessitates a direct data retrieval and export approach. A batch script querying the target data source seems the appropriate solution, circumventing the need to interact with the Excel file. The goal is to produce a TSV file containing the verified company data for immediate user consumption.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Test script to fetch 5 items from bizno.net","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"const fs = require('fs');\n\nasync function fetchBiznoInfo(bizno) {\n  try {\n    const res = await fetch(`https://bizno.net/article/${bizno}`, {\n      headers: {\n        'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/120.0.0.0 Safari/537.36'\n      }\n    });\n    if (!res.ok) return { bizno, error: res.status };\n    const html = await res.text();\n    \n    // Parse fields\n    const data = { bizno };\n    \n    // Title / Company\n    const titleMatch = html.match(/<title>(.*?)<\\/title>/i);\n    if (titleMatch) {\n      data.company = titleMatch[1].replace(/[-|].*$/, '').trim();\n    }\n    \n    // Status\n    if (html.includes('폐업자')) data.status = '폐업';\n    else if (html.includes('휴업자')) data.status = '휴업';\n    else if (html.includes('계속사업자')) data.status = '정상';\n    else data.status = '';\n\n    // Zip code\n    const zipMatch = html.match(/우편번호\\s*<\\/th>\\s*<td[^>]*>\\s*(\\d{5})\\s*<\\/td>/i) ||\n                     html.match(/우편번호[\\s\\S]*?(\\d{5})/);\n    if (zipMatch) data.zip = zipMatch[1];\n    \n    // Employee count\n    const empMatch = html.match(/종업원수\\s*<\\/th>\\s*<td[^>]*>\\s*([^<]+)<\\/td>/i) ||\n                     html.match(/종업원수[\\s\\S]*?([0-9,]+명)/);\n    if (empMatch) data.employees = empMatch[1].replace(/[^0-9]/g, '');\n\n    // Classifications\n    const daeMatch = html.match(/대분류\\s*:\\s*([^<\\n\\r]+?)(?=\\s*중분류|$)/);\n    const jungMatch = html.match(/중분류\\s*:\\s*([^<\\n\\r]+?)(?=\\s*소분류|$)/);\n    const soMatch = html.match(/소분류\\s*:\\s*([^<\\n\\r]+?)(?=\\s*세분류|$)/);\n    if (daeMatch) data.dae = daeMatch[1].trim();\n    if (jungMatch) data.jung = jungMatch[1].trim();\n    if (soMatch) data.so = soMatch[1].trim();\n    \n    // Industry (종목)\n    const indMatch = html.match(/종\\s*목\\s*<\\/th>\\s*<td[^>]*>\\s*([^<]+)<\\/td>/i) ||\n                     html.match(/업종\\s*:\\s*([^<\\n\\r]+)/);\n    if (indMatch) data.industry = indMatch[1].trim();\n\n    return data;\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { bizno, error: err.message };\n  }\n}\n\nasync function runTest() {\n  const testBiznos = ['6090653247', '6090657239', '6090657409', '6090658771', '6090848296'];\n  for (const b of testBiznos) {\n    const t0 = Date.now();\n    const info = await fetchBiznoInfo(b);\n    console.log(`Bizno ${b} (${Date.now() - t0}ms):`, info);\n  }\n}\n\nrunTest();\n","Description":"Test fetching 5 bizno items","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\e1493fa0-e8a4-4717-a46c-5bc1b3357473\\scratch\\test_fetch5.js","toolAction":"Creating test fetch script","toolSummary":"Write test_fetch5.js"}}]}
